---
/**
 * "How this will work for real candidates": what exists today (Stage 1 e-mail form only), what Stage 2 adds, and the
 * document states of APPLICATION_SYSTEM_SPEC §8.3 / §12.3. Stage 2 is gated by the owner's sign-off (§11).
 */
import { STATES, STATE_LABELS, STATE_NOTES } from '../../lib/readiness.mjs';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
interface Props { /** Real records that have completed verification (published). */ publishedCount: number }
const { publishedCount } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="how" aria-labelledby="how-h">
  <h2 id="how-h">How this will work for real candidates</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p><strong>None of this exists for real candidates yet.</strong> Today the “{SITE.cta}” form sends your details to us by e-mail, and we keep a private copy of the enquiry. That is all it does. There are no accounts, no saved profiles, no uploads, no status tracking and no payments.</p>
    <p>A real check will compare only requirements we have verified on the university's official page, each with its source and the date we read it.{publishedCount === 0 && ' No university record on this site has completed verification yet, so no real comparison can be shown.'}</p>
    <p>Accounts, saved profiles and secure uploads belong to Stage 2. Stage 2 is gated: it starts only after the owner signs off account security, upload handling, abuse controls, backups, retention and deletion, the privacy notice and an access review (APPLICATION_SYSTEM_SPEC.md §11). Until then, please do not send scans of your passport or certificates.</p>
    <h3>Document states after Stage 2</h3>
    <ol class="states">
      {STATES.map((s) => (
        <li data-state-step={s}><strong>{STATE_LABELS[s]}.</strong> {STATE_NOTES[s]}</li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="small">An item that needs a replacement or clarification goes back to “outstanding” with the reason shown. If the programme or intake changes, items that are no longer needed move to “not requested”; nothing is deleted.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .how { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .states { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .states li { margin-bottom: .4rem; }
  .small { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--slate); }
</style>
